#: src/macros/proc-macros/in-the-wild.md:6
msgid "Procedural Macros In The Wild"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/in-the-wild.md:8
msgid ""
"Many of the most popular and foundational libraries in the Rust ecosystem "
"rely heavily on procedural macros to provide elegant, declarative, and type-"
"safe APIs:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/in-the-wild.md:12
msgid ""
"**Serde (`#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize)]`):** Automatically generates "
"code to convert Rust types to/from JSON, YAML, or binary formats based on "
"field names and structural nesting."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/in-the-wild.md:15
msgid ""
"**Tokio (`#[tokio::main]`):** Sets up runtime environments, wrapping "
"standard main entry points asynchronously."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/in-the-wild.md:17
msgid ""
"**Clap (`#[derive(Parser)]`):** Automatically builds complete, robust CLI "
"command-line argument parsers based on struct declarations and doc comments."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/in-the-wild.md:19
msgid ""
"**SQLx (`query!`):** Validates SQL query strings against a live database at "
"build time, converting database schemas directly to static Rust types."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/in-the-wild.md:25
msgid ""
"Highlight the impact of procedural macros for Rust's ergonomics--"
"serialization, for example, requires explicit compiler support in many "
"languages."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/in-the-wild.md:28
msgid ""
"SQLx's compile-time query verification is a prime example of compile-time "
"code validation that is only possible with procedural macros."
msgstr ""
